        {
          "step": "3",
          "title": "KANGAROO SPRING NETWORK",
          "text": "KANGAROO SPRING NETWORK\r\nIn this example, Kangaroo is used to create a spring network from a mesh and then relax\r\nthe network under a constant force. The Kangaroo Zombie solver is used to avoid having\r\ncalculation loops in Grasshopper.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "Isotrim",
            "Divide Domain²",
            "Cull Pattern",
            "Mesh Brep",
            "Plane Surface",
            "Distance",
            "Mesh Join",
            "Area"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
            589.2,
            644.4
          ]
        },
        {
          "step": "4",
          "title": "FIELD FROM KANGAROO",
          "text": "FIELD FROM KANGAROO\r\nThe resulting mesh is used to generate a distance field, driving the aggregation\r\nto grow along the mesh itself.\r\nA graph mapper is used to sharpen the transition between values in the field.",
          "nearby_components": [
            "NumberSlider",
            "NumberSlider",
            "Scale NU",
            "Bounding Box",
            "Volume",
            "Point List"
          ],
          "annotation_type": "Scribble",
          "pos": [
